WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:15.240
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:19.529
online retreat. We've reached session

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:24.660
number nine, and this is going to be a

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:27.390
meditation. And some of you have done

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:35.520
this meditation before during the Lion's

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:39.800
Dance meditation. But we're about to

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.800
discuss the Wheel of Life in detail.

00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:46.620
We've been talking about how to go from

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:55.710
one life to another life, especially the

00:00:46.620 --> 00:01:01.170
bardo (BAR DO). And now we're going to explore

00:00:55.710 --> 00:01:07.229
that. By the way, I made a mistake in

00:01:01.170 --> 00:01:10.830
the video yesterday, and I would like to

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:18.180
correct it. So there are two books about

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:22.979
how to help somebody in the bardo. And

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:27.450
the two names are very similar, and I

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:33.840
made a mistake yesterday. So the first

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:36.329
book is called bardo tu drul (BAR DO THOS GROL), which means "just

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:46.320
hearing about it you can be liberated in

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:48.780
the bardo." And that's the book which is

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:51.770
not considered authentic in our

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:51.770
Tsongkapa tradition,

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:03.530
and it has been translated in English as

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:11.360
the "Tibetan Book of the Dead" or names

00:02:03.530 --> 00:02:15.380
like that. So I would encourage you to

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:27.020
rather use the great ancient books on

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:35.300
the Abhidharma, and that's the presentation I made

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:37.160
in this course. The book name I used

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:44.510
yesterday, which is bardo trang drul (BAR DO 'PHRANG SGROL)-- 

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:56.290
one word difference ... that means

00:02:44.510 --> 00:03:00.290
"freedom from the narrow alleyway of the bardo." And

00:02:56.290 --> 00:03:07.130
that's a great book. So I made a mistake

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:09.320
yesterday; I mentioned that book and that

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:17.030
that's a pretty famous jang chok (BYANG CHOG) or

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:19.310
"how to help somebody in the bardo." Also

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:23.269
yesterday, or a few days ago, we mentioned

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:35.570
the word bum ('BUM), like in Milarepa's "One Hundred

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:37.790
Songs." And the usual name of his book is...

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:44.690
the nickname is gur bum (MGUR 'BUM). gur  

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:51.019
bum. So literally it means "one-hundred thousand

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:53.720
songs," but the "hundred thousand" just

00:03:51.019 --> 00:03:56.440
means "a collection" of his songs; it's not

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.440
a hundred thousand.

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:06.380
There's a similar word sungbum (GSUNG 'BUM), which

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:20.239
means the collected works of any modern

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:22.760
Tibetan in the last one thousand years. So we

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:24.410
kind of... I think we translated it as "one hundred"

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:31.190
and not "one-hundred thousand," so it should be

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:34.520
translated as "one-hundred thousand." Okay, so we're going to

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:37.040
go through a meditation which is part of

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:39.770
the ancient Lion's Dance meditation, which

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:52.040
was taught by Buddha, and also Maitreya

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:58.280
and Asanga. And we're going to go on a

00:04:52.040 --> 00:05:01.490
journey to our past life. But the purpose

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:07.490
of that is to explore dependence - or you

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:09.169
can call it dependent origination - which

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:17.270
is the meaning of the twelve links

00:05:09.169 --> 00:05:19.250
inside the Wheel of Life. We're going to be

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:21.020
going deep into those twelve links

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:29.750
starting with the next session, session

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:31.310
ten. And there's a way that you can

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:41.900
explore them personally during a

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:45.280
meditation. So let's do that together. I'm going to put

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.280
on my meditation timer.

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:55.159
This is a nice timer. I would use it -

00:05:50.120 --> 00:06:02.990
it's called Insight Timer. Okay, here we

00:05:55.159 --> 00:06:07.370
go. Get comfortable on your seat. A little

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:13.159
bit of a smile. Of course there are serious

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:15.319
things happening in the world, but it

00:06:13.159 --> 00:06:22.909
doesn't mean we have to go around with a

00:06:15.319 --> 00:06:29.419
scowl on our mouths. These are the kind of times when

00:06:22.909 --> 00:06:37.879
people need a smile, and they need us to

00:06:29.419 --> 00:06:45.740
be friendly and warm towards them. Relax

00:06:37.879 --> 00:06:48.349
your forehead. Relax your fingers. During

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:52.749
the meditation, try not to tighten your

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:52.749
forehead or get wrinkles on your forehead.

00:07:00.279 --> 00:07:10.819
Personally, I find it very useful to

00:07:02.899 --> 00:07:15.159
have a slight smile. The eyes are closed,

00:07:10.819 --> 00:07:15.159
but they are focused a little bit up. And

00:07:17.139 --> 00:07:29.509
it's very good to tighten the lower

00:07:19.969 --> 00:07:32.050
abdomen, which strengthens the back. So

00:07:29.509 --> 00:07:32.050
here we go.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:41.120
We're going to start this meditation with

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:46.370
ten breaths. So let's count ten slow

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:47.870
breaths. By tradition, the out-breath...

00:07:46.370 --> 00:07:54.350
the beginning of the breath is the

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:56.210
out-breath. And remember that I'm asking

00:07:54.350 --> 00:08:05.840
you at the end of your out-breath to

00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:08.630
push out a little more air. Let's enjoy ten

00:08:05.840 --> 00:08:11.560
long exhale breaths. The inhale will take

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:11.560
care of itself.

00:09:22.279 --> 00:09:35.839
And we'll do a quick seven-step

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:39.550
preliminary. So please invite one of your

00:09:35.839 --> 00:09:39.550
teachers to come and sit in front of you.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:55.829
Now let's make them a gift of

00:10:53.189 --> 00:11:05.970
appreciation of some great quality of

00:10:55.829 --> 00:11:09.259
theirs. Think of something about your

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.259
teacher that you really admire.

00:12:30.570 --> 00:12:40.200
Now let's clean some bad seeds from

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:46.770
yesterday. Think of two or three mistakes

00:12:40.200 --> 00:12:50.300
you made yesterday, and open up your

00:12:46.770 --> 00:12:50.300
heart and admit them to your teacher.

00:12:51.950 --> 00:13:00.170
Make a promise not to repeat them for

00:12:57.240 --> 00:13:00.170
some length of time.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:11.389
Now give equal time and energy to

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:14.980
thinking about a few good things you did

00:14:11.389 --> 00:14:14.980
yesterday and telling your teacher.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:27.749
Now as for teachings in your life, some

00:15:25.589 --> 00:15:29.609
of them will come as positive

00:15:27.749 --> 00:15:32.269
teachings and some of them will come as

00:15:29.609 --> 00:15:32.269
challenges.

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:43.399
Now ask your teacher to please stay in

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:46.879
your life. You can see a big difference

00:16:43.399 --> 00:16:49.959
between people who have a close

00:16:46.879 --> 00:16:49.959
teacher and people who don't.

00:16:57.639 --> 00:17:02.829
If we're lucky, we have a teacher we can

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:02.829
be close to.

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:12.810
Now let's go back to the beginning of

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:19.170
these preliminary steps. We are looking at

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:21.720
the teacher in front of us. Again, they

00:18:19.170 --> 00:18:32.070
are alive and they are warm - they are a

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:36.320
real person. Now try to imagine something

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:36.320
about them that you really appreciate.

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:50.250
The reason they're your teacher is they

00:18:48.030 --> 00:18:57.750
know something that you would like

00:18:50.250 --> 00:19:00.300
to learn. They have certain habits or

00:18:57.750 --> 00:19:09.270
certain skills that we would like to

00:19:00.300 --> 00:19:15.900
learn. So think about just any one of

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:21.360
those. Why are you... why did you choose

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:28.710
them as a teacher? What do they have that

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:36.330
you don't have? What did they have that you

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:38.780
want to learn? Think about one thing - one

00:19:36.330 --> 00:19:38.780
good quality.

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:57.840
Now think, "The reason I see this good

00:20:51.059 --> 00:21:08.520
quality," if we go back to the the old

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:10.890
popular pen teaching ... "because a dog and a

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:19.860
human see a pen as a different thing

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:30.809
that shows that the pen is coming from

00:21:19.860 --> 00:21:35.630
the human's mind and the same object is

00:21:30.809 --> 00:21:35.630
being seen as a chew toy by the dog.

00:21:37.789 --> 00:21:47.250
Therefore, the pen is not coming from the

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:49.679
pen. If the pen was coming from the

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:58.950
pen, then both the dog and the human would

00:21:49.679 --> 00:22:04.140
see it as a pen. And the reason the human

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:09.240
sees a pen is that they have a seed in

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:18.600
their mind, and when they look at the

00:22:09.240 --> 00:22:20.640
cylinder stick--the pen stick--when they

00:22:18.600 --> 00:22:23.149
look on those parts, then the seed opens

00:22:20.640 --> 00:22:23.149
in their mind

00:22:25.750 --> 00:22:41.320
and an image made of light comes out of

00:22:30.770 --> 00:22:41.320
the seed and it settles down on the pen--

00:22:41.470 --> 00:22:55.700
on the cylinder--and that's why the human

00:22:48.620 --> 00:23:02.780
sees a pen." Now, how that seed got into

00:22:55.700 --> 00:23:06.820
the human's mind--karmic seed--we're going

00:23:02.780 --> 00:23:06.820
to explore that during the Wheel of Life.

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:22.610
But we all know, "because of the first law

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:25.070
of karma--watermelons make watermelons--if

00:23:22.610 --> 00:23:32.300
I see an instrument of communication

00:23:25.070 --> 00:23:38.960
like a pen and that comes out of a

00:23:32.300 --> 00:23:41.990
karmic seed in my mind, then I must have

00:23:38.960 --> 00:23:49.160
helped some other people communicate in

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:51.050
the past. That also applies to the

00:23:49.160 --> 00:24:00.380
beautiful quality I see in my teacher

00:23:51.050 --> 00:24:06.820
right now. It's coming from a seed in my

00:24:00.380 --> 00:24:10.520
mind. And because of the laws of karma,

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:14.890
what I did to plant the seed is similar

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:14.890
to how I see my lama acting now.

00:24:21.019 --> 00:24:33.269
So this sweet quality that I see in my

00:24:24.029 --> 00:24:36.929
lama nowadays--that's coming out of a

00:24:33.269 --> 00:24:52.409
seed that I planted by behaving like him

00:24:36.929 --> 00:24:54.539
or her in my past lives. If I experienced

00:24:52.409 --> 00:25:04.349
my teacher as a very patient person--no

00:24:54.539 --> 00:25:06.899
anger--then it must be that in one of my

00:25:04.349 --> 00:25:13.409
past lives I was a person who didn't

00:25:06.899 --> 00:25:16.009
have much anger." So we're going to go on

00:25:13.409 --> 00:25:24.779
sort of an exploration--a detective

00:25:16.009 --> 00:25:31.859
exploration. "That quality that I see in

00:25:24.779 --> 00:25:34.950
my teacher"--the patience, for example--"it must

00:25:31.859 --> 00:25:42.090
have been planted by me, myself, in a

00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:49.529
past life." So let's go on an exploration to

00:25:42.090 --> 00:25:55.139
our past life--just in our imagination.

00:25:49.529 --> 00:25:56.909
And not many of us in this world have

00:25:55.139 --> 00:25:59.509
the ability to see our past lives

00:25:56.909 --> 00:25:59.509
directly,

00:26:05.200 --> 00:26:17.590
but it's fun to guess, "What did I do in

00:26:08.590 --> 00:26:25.630
the past to see this?" Then use your

00:26:17.590 --> 00:26:27.910
imagination, have fun, enjoy! We're trying

00:26:25.630 --> 00:26:36.130
to find powerful good seeds in our

00:26:27.910 --> 00:26:44.950
past lives. And make a movie in your mind.

00:26:36.130 --> 00:26:50.010
"Oh, in my past life I was 

00:26:44.950 --> 00:26:50.010
threatened by some other country's army,

00:26:51.870 --> 00:27:05.470
but I was very patient and I refused to

00:26:57.010 --> 00:27:07.020
fight. I refused to be angry." Then for the

00:27:05.470 --> 00:27:15.700
movie, you're going to have to 

00:27:07.020 --> 00:27:21.039
decide what country you were in, and what

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:25.929
body were you in. Were you a man or were

00:27:21.039 --> 00:27:33.700
you a woman? What race of people or culture of

00:27:25.929 --> 00:27:35.440
people were you? Was it last year or was

00:27:33.700 --> 00:27:46.289
it a hundred years ago, or a thousand

00:27:35.440 --> 00:27:46.289
years ago? So make this beautiful story.

00:27:46.830 --> 00:27:56.229
Don't be shy. And make it sweet. If

00:27:54.009 --> 00:27:57.190
you have a teacher in this life, or you

00:27:56.229 --> 00:28:07.899
can even imagine an

00:27:57.190 --> 00:28:09.759
historical teacher in front of you, if

00:28:07.899 --> 00:28:12.220
you even heard in this life the word

00:28:09.759 --> 00:28:20.399
"Buddha," or the word "Mohammed," or the

00:28:12.220 --> 00:28:23.190
word "Jesus," it means you're a good person

00:28:20.399 --> 00:28:28.479
and you had some extraordinary

00:28:23.190 --> 00:28:33.340
experiences in your past life. So we're

00:28:28.479 --> 00:28:45.009
going to go on a pretended exploration of

00:28:33.340 --> 00:28:47.739
our past life. Just enjoy. Make it detailed--

00:28:45.009 --> 00:28:51.309
don't say, "Oh, I was patient."  Try

00:28:47.739 --> 00:28:54.190
to imagine someone... specific kind of

00:28:51.309 --> 00:28:58.320
person, "looks like this, tried to hit me, I

00:28:54.190 --> 00:28:58.320
was patient." Okay?

00:29:10.859 --> 00:29:22.559
Recently in my own case, if I just imagined

00:29:17.769 --> 00:29:22.559
my past life--I cannot see it directly--I

00:29:24.450 --> 00:29:34.440
keep getting a woman from the Middle

00:29:28.149 --> 00:29:40.629
East. And, I don't know, maybe it was

00:29:34.440 --> 00:29:45.340
a thousand years ago and she's a physician--

00:29:40.629 --> 00:29:51.220
she's a doctor. Then I make a whole story

00:29:45.340 --> 00:29:54.789
about this physician. So you'll see the

00:29:51.220 --> 00:30:02.580
the photograph... I put it as the header

00:29:54.789 --> 00:30:05.799
for this class. I found a picture of...

00:30:02.580 --> 00:30:17.679
I found a picture online who looked

00:30:05.799 --> 00:30:20.349
like her. So let's imagine. Have fun. Don't

00:30:17.679 --> 00:30:22.749
get stuck. Don't stop--if we still have

00:30:20.349 --> 00:30:33.519
more time, then slow down and make a nice

00:30:22.749 --> 00:30:39.009
story. This is an exercise in the Wheel

00:30:33.519 --> 00:30:45.009
of Life. This is an exercise in dependent

00:30:39.009 --> 00:30:49.029
origination. The Shalistambha Sutra

00:30:45.009 --> 00:30:54.669
said--and we're going to talk about it

00:30:49.029 --> 00:31:01.139
next class--Buddha said, "If you see

00:30:54.669 --> 00:31:01.139
something, then something made it happen."

00:31:01.619 --> 00:31:08.739
So, let's have fun. We'll take about ten

00:31:06.759 --> 00:31:11.329
minutes.

00:31:08.739 --> 00:31:19.159
If you get tired, if you forget what

00:31:11.329 --> 00:31:24.469
you're doing, just come back. Keep adding

00:31:19.159 --> 00:31:31.249
more and more detail. Are you seeing your

00:31:24.469 --> 00:31:38.329
past life directly? I think in my case,

00:31:31.249 --> 00:31:44.019
and most of us, we are not. Are we just

00:31:38.329 --> 00:31:50.599
imagining our past life? Yeah, we are.

00:31:44.019 --> 00:31:57.709
But don't forget, even a movie you

00:31:50.599 --> 00:32:01.959
imagine in your mind, those imaginations

00:31:57.709 --> 00:32:01.959
in your mind are also coming from seeds.

00:32:04.059 --> 00:32:16.429
You cannot imagine patience of a woman a

00:32:09.049 --> 00:32:22.399
thousand years ago if you don't have

00:32:16.429 --> 00:32:29.839
seeds for patience. In that sense, higher

00:32:22.399 --> 00:32:33.319
Middle Way school, they would say this

00:32:29.839 --> 00:32:46.190
movie we are pretending has some

00:32:33.319 --> 00:32:51.859
reality. OK. Let's go. Let's enjoy. Choose a

00:32:46.190 --> 00:32:56.899
beautiful quality of your teacher. Make a

00:32:51.859 --> 00:33:03.699
beautiful story--hundred years ago, a

00:32:56.899 --> 00:33:03.699
thousand years ago, any country you want,

00:33:03.760 --> 00:33:14.380
any person you want to be collected the

00:33:09.559 --> 00:33:14.380
seeds to see this lama in my life now.

00:33:18.580 --> 00:33:22.030
Okay, let's go.

00:39:04.500 --> 00:39:07.970
Now slowly come back.

00:39:14.530 --> 00:39:21.670
Come back to the teacher sitting in

00:39:16.390 --> 00:39:25.920
front of you. Look at that same good

00:39:21.670 --> 00:39:25.920
quality, but now appreciate it differently.

00:39:28.650 --> 00:39:44.310
"In a way, it's part of me already. I still

00:39:40.150 --> 00:39:44.310
have that quality also--some of it."

00:39:57.730 --> 00:40:03.840
Dedicate the good karma of this

00:39:59.650 --> 00:40:03.840
meditation--the seventh preliminary.

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:19.900
Pray that all people could plant good

00:40:12.160 --> 00:40:22.890
seeds like this one. Imagine a whole

00:40:19.900 --> 00:40:22.890
world of people like that.

00:40:33.660 --> 00:40:48.900
Then you can slowly open your eyes. Take a

00:40:38.789 --> 00:40:53.730
stretch. That's dependent origination. It

00:40:48.900 --> 00:40:56.130
will lead us into emptiness and that

00:40:53.730 --> 00:40:58.650
emptiness will help us in the first of

00:40:56.130 --> 00:41:10.920
the twelve steps of the wheel of dependent

00:40:58.650 --> 00:41:13.160
origination. See you in session ten. Thank you,

00:41:10.920 --> 00:41:13.160
Stanley!

